[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]

; THE CLUSTER MINE, AS THE SQUAD USES IT.
;
; Thrown further out than the heavy one (12 m rather than 7) because it does not
; land as a mine — it bursts and scatters five proximity submines over about six
; metres, so what it is really placing is a patch of ground, and the patch wants
; to be on the approach rather than underfoot.
;
; Its submines stay for the mission, as the Heavy Mine does. min_contact_metres
; 14 is still a little further out than the heavy mine's, but for a different
; reason now: five bomblets scattered over six metres need the room to land and
; settle before anything walks into the patch, and nothing about laying one early
; is wasted any more.
;
; cooldown is short for a mine because quantity is 4: the item is a field, and a
; robot that can only lay one every forty seconds never builds one.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Character/characters/ai/equipment/ai_mine.gd" id="1_mine"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://Character/weapon/mines/mine_cluster_canister.tscn" id="2_canister"]

